db_erd_returns", "label": "returns table", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "db/ERD.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "db_erd_return_events", "label": "return_events table", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "db/ERD.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "db_erd_mark_coverage", "label": "mark_coverage view", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "db/ERD.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Exposes person x week cells with no mark: the workbook #DIV/0! problem stated as a query."}, {"id": "db_erd_return_turnaround", "label": "return_turnaround view", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "db/ERD.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "db_erd_return_stage_gaps", "label": "return_stage_gaps view", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "db/ERD.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Orders by chain position, not date, so two stages on the same day still read forwards."}, {"id": "db_erd_mark_context_snapshot", "label": "Marks snapshot their context (branch_id, form_key)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "db/ERD.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "People transfer branches and change roles; a mark must stay attached to the branch and form it was scored under or historical reports silently rewrite themselves."}, {"id": "db_erd_generated_pct_column", "label": "Generated pct column (never stored as input)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "db/ERD.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "marks.pct = total_score/max_score generated so a score cannot disagree with its lines; fixes the workbook defect where a percentage cell outlived its numbers."}, {"id": "db_erd_derived_ageing", "label": "Ageing is derived, never stored", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "db/ERD.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "return_events records what happened and when; turnaround and stage gaps are computed, e.g. now() - opened_on."}, {"id": "db_erd_missing_rows_meaningful", "label": "Missing rows are meaningful", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "db/ERD.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Gaps are data; mark_coverage returns 32 of 44 gaps for Machang and 12 of 16 for Kota Bharu on the seed."}, {"id": "db_erd_workbook_div0_problem", "label": "Workbook #DIV/0! problem", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "db/ERD.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "db_erd_security_invoker_views", "label": "security_invoker views (Postgres 15+)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "db/ERD.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Without security_invoker a view runs as its owner and quietly bypasses every RLS policy; this is why Postgres 15+ is required."}, {"id": "db_erd_rls_branch_scoping", "label": "RLS branch scoping", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "db/ERD.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Scoping enforced by RLS not the client: a supervisor querying another outlet gets zero rows. Admin cross-branch, everyone else own branch_id, reference tables readable by any signed-in user."}, {"id": "db_erd_security_definer_helpers", "label": "SECURITY DEFINER RLS helpers (auth bridge)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "db/ERD.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Branch scoping needs caller's branch_id from users, the table the policy guards; reading it directly re-enters its own policy. SECURITY DEFINER runs that lookup outside RLS; search_path pinned to block escalation."}, {"id": "db_erd_app_can_see_branch", "label": "app_can_see_branch(text)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "db/ERD.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Single predicate every scoped policy calls; change the scoping rule in one place, not twenty policies."}, {"id": "db_erd_permissive_rls_fails_silently", "label": "Permissive RLS fails silently", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "db/ERD.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Wrong policies still return rows, just the wrong ones; so tests assert what each role cannot read."}, {"id": "db_erd_stage_ownership_not_security", "label": "Stage ownership is not a security boundary", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "db/ERD.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Which of store or clerk records which return step stays in the app; DB enforces branch and role."}, {"id": "db_erd_rls_test_suite", "label": "supabase/tests/rls.test.mjs (npm run test:rls)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "db/ERD.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "db_erd_pglite", "label": "PGlite (Postgres engine for tests)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "db/ERD.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "db_erd_init_migration", "label": "